/-!
# The restriction of a dualizing module to an effective Cartier divisor

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, let `D ⊆ X` be an effective Cartier divisor with closed
immersion `i : D ⟶ X`, and let `ω` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module which, placed in some
cohomological degree, is a dualizing complex on `X` ([Stacks, Tag 0A87]). This file proves that
`i^*ω` placed in degree one is a dualizing complex on `D`, so that `i^*ω` is a dualizing module
on `D` in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 0B4R].

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.isDualizingComplex_single_one_pullback` — `i^*ω` in degree one is a dualizing
  complex on `D`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isDualizingModule_pullback` — `i^*ω` is a dualizing module on `D`.

## The proof

Being a dualizing complex is a condition on affine opens, and
`Stacks.Duality.isDualizingComplex_single_of_forall_exists_module_iso` reduces it to exhibiting,
through every point of `D`, an affine open together with a module over its ring of sections which
presents the restriction there and which is a dualizing complex.

Through a point of `D` take an affine open `U ⊆ X` on which the ideal of `D` is generated by a
single nonzerodivisor `f`, which is what being an effective Cartier divisor supplies
(`Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`). Then `i⁻¹(U)`
is affine, the ring map `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(D, i⁻¹U)` is surjective with kernel the ideal generated by
`f` (`Stacks.Divisors.surjective_chartHom` and `Stacks.Divisors.ker_chartHom`, which are the
sections description of a closed subscheme read at a chart of the divisor), and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictedPullbackModelIso` presents `(i^*ω)|_{i⁻¹U}` by the
extension of scalars of `ω(U)` along that ring map. That extension of scalars, placed in degree
one, is a dualizing complex over `Γ(D, i⁻¹U)` by
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_single_extendScalars_of_ker_eq_span_singleton`, whose two module
inputs are available at the chart: `ω(U)` in degree zero is a dualizing complex over `Γ(X, U)`
(`Stacks.Duality.isDualizingComplex_single_specModule`), and `f` is a nonzerodivisor on `ω(U)`
because it is one on `Γ(X, U)` (`Dualizing.isSMulRegular_of_isDualizingComplex_single`).

Coherence of `i^*ω`, the other half of being a dualizing module, is read off the conclusion
itself: the cohomology sheaves of a dualizing complex are coherent.

## Implementation notes

The ring map at a chart is written `i.appLE U (i⁻¹U) le_rfl` rather than `i.app U`, because that
is the spelling in which the affine comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictedPullbackModelIso` produces the presenting module; the
two agree by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app`, which is how the surjectivity and the
kernel are transported from Mathlib's `app` form.

`IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme` is not an instance, so it is introduced by a `letI` in the
statements below; it holds because a closed subscheme of a locally Noetherian scheme is locally
Noetherian.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A87](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A87)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AX0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AX0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE (specModule)

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace Stacks.Duality

/-- **Being a dualizing module depends on the module only through its isomorphism class.** Both
halves are invariant: coherence by `AlgebraicGeometry.isCoherent_of_moduleIso`, and the
dualizing-complex condition because the single-degree functor carries an isomorphism of modules
to one of `D(𝒪_X)`. -/
theorem isDualizingModule_of_iso {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] {ω ω' : Y.Modules}
    (e : ω ≅ ω') (h : IsDualizingModule ω) : IsDualizingModule ω' := by
  obtain ⟨hcoh, n, hn⟩ := h
  exact ⟨AlgebraicGeometry.isCoherent_of_moduleIso e hcoh, n,
    isDualizingComplex_of_iso ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules n).mapIso e) hn⟩

end Stacks.Duality

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData)

/-! ### The ring map at a chart of the divisor -/

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian X] in
/-- **The ring map on sections at a chart of a closed subscheme is surjective.** This is
Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeι_app_surjective`, read on the
spelling `i.appLE U (i⁻¹U) le_rfl` of the map. -/
theorem surjective_chartHom {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Function.Surjective (D.subschemeι.appLE U (D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app]
  exact D.subschemeι_app_surjective ⟨U, hU⟩

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian X] in
/-- **At a chart on which the ideal of the divisor is generated by one element, the ring map on
sections has that element as its kernel.** This is Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app` together with the hypothesis that
the ideal is principal there. -/
theorem ker_chartHom {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)}
    (hgen : D.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span {f}) :
    RingHom.ker (D.subschemeι.appLE U (D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom = Ideal.span {f} := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app, D.ker_subschemeι_app ⟨U, hU⟩, hgen]

/-! ### The chart-level dualizing complex -/

/-- **The sections of a dualizing module at an affine open, and the regularity of a
nonzerodivisor on them.** Over an affine open `U` of a locally Noetherian scheme the sections of
`ω` placed in degree zero are a dualizing complex over `Γ(X, U)`, and an element of `Γ(X, U)`
which is a nonzerodivisor is a nonzerodivisor on them. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_specModule_and_isSMulRegular (ω : X.Modules) [ω.IsQuasicoherent]
    (n : ℤ) (hω : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules n).obj ω))
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)} (hf : IsRegular f) :
    letI : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
    Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U)) 0).obj (specModule ω hU)) ∧
      IsSMulRegular (specModule ω hU) f := by
  let : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
  have h0 := Stacks.Duality.isDualizingComplex_single_specModule ω n hω U hU
  exact ⟨h0, Dualizing.isSMulRegular_of_isDualizingComplex_single _ 0 h0 f
    (isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mp hf)⟩

/-- **The presenting module of `i^*ω` at a chart of the divisor is a dualizing complex.** Over an
affine open `U ⊆ X` on which the ideal of `D` is generated by a nonzerodivisor `f`, the extension
of scalars of `ω(U)` along `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(D, i⁻¹U)`, placed in degree one, is a dualizing complex:
the ring map is surjective with kernel `(f)`, so this is
`Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_single_extendScalars_of_ker_eq_span_singleton`. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_single_one_extendScalars_chartHom (ω : X.Modules)
    [ω.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℤ) (hω : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules n).obj ω))
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)} (hf : IsRegular f)
    (hgen : D.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span {f}) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme := D.isLocallyNoetherian_subscheme
    letI : IsNoetherianRing Γ(D.subscheme, D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) :=
      IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian
        ⟨D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U, hU.preimage D.subschemeι⟩
    Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(D.subscheme, D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U)) 1).obj
        ((ModuleCat.extendScalars
          (D.subschemeι.appLE U (D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom).obj (specModule ω hU))) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme := D.isLocallyNoetherian_subscheme
  let : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
  let : IsNoetherianRing Γ(D.subscheme, D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) :=
    IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian
      ⟨D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U, hU.preimage D.subschemeι⟩
  obtain ⟨hdual, hreg⟩ :=
    isDualizingComplex_specModule_and_isSMulRegular ω n hω hU hf
  exact Dualizing.isDualizingComplex_single_extendScalars_of_ker_eq_span_singleton
    (D.subschemeι.appLE U (D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom (surjective_chartHom D hU) f
    (isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mp hf) (ker_chartHom D hU hgen)
    (specModule ω hU) 0 hdual hreg

/-! ### The restriction to the divisor -/

variable [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D]

/-- **The restriction of a dualizing module to an effective Cartier divisor is a dualizing
complex in degree one.** If `ω` is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module which placed in degree `n` is a
dualizing complex on `X`, then `i^*ω` placed in degree one is a dualizing complex on `D`. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_single_one_pullback (ω : X.Modules) [ω.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℤ)
    (hω : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules n).obj ω)) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme := D.isLocallyNoetherian_subscheme
    Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor D.subscheme.Modules 1).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback D.subschemeι).obj ω)) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme := D.isLocallyNoetherian_subscheme
  refine Stacks.Duality.isDualizingComplex_single_of_forall_exists_module_iso _ 1 fun y => ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hyU, f, hfreg, hgen⟩ :=
    exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor D ‹_›
      (D.subschemeι.base y)
  refine ⟨D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U, hU.preimage D.subschemeι, hyU,
    (ModuleCat.extendScalars
      (D.subschemeι.appLE U (D.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom).obj (specModule ω hU), ?_,
    isDualizingComplex_single_one_extendScalars_chartHom D ω n hω hU hfreg hgen⟩
  exact Scheme.Modules.restrictedPullbackModelIso D.subschemeι hU
      (hU.preimage D.subschemeι) le_rfl ω ≪≫
    eqToIso (Functor.comp_obj _ _ _).symm

/-- **The restriction of a dualizing module to an effective Cartier divisor is a dualizing
module.** Coherence is the coherence of the degree-one cohomology sheaf of the dualizing complex
of `Stacks.Divisors.isDualizingComplex_single_one_pullback`. -/
theorem isDualizingModule_pullback (ω : X.Modules) [ω.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℤ)
    (hω : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules n).obj ω)) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme := D.isLocallyNoetherian_subscheme
    Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingModule ((Scheme.Modules.pullback D.subschemeι).obj ω) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian D.subscheme := D.isLocallyNoetherian_subscheme
  have hd := isDualizingComplex_single_one_pullback D ω n hω
  refine ⟨?_, 1, hd⟩
  have hcoh := Stacks.Duality.isCoherent_homology_of_isDualizingComplex hd 1
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.isCoherent_of_moduleIso
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorCompHomologyFunctorIso D.subscheme.Modules 1).app _) hcoh

end Stacks.Divisors

end
